    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-gray-900 tracking-tight mb-3">
      French Drain Pipe: Should Holes Face UP or DOWN?
    </h1>
    <p class="text-base text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-6">
      Ask five different DIY homeowners or amateur handymen whether the perforated holes on a French drain pipe should face up or down, and you will start a heated argument. But in civil engineering and municipal drainage manuals, there is no debate whatsoever: <strong>the holes must ALWAYS face DOWN</strong>. Here is the physical science behind how groundwater actually behaves.
    </p>

    <!-- Quick Stats Grid -->
